{
 "_note": "Chromium at deviceScaleFactor 2, one clean database per width. The admin is a two-pane layout: the page does not scroll, #content does, so contentScrollWidth/contentClientWidth are the numbers that see a horizontal overflow -- document.documentElement.scrollWidth stays at the viewport width however wide a child is. widestChild is the widest element inside the column. Measured from the real layout; the photographs were then taken with the column unclipped so a tall screen fits in one image.",
 "_server": "This machine has no ffmpeg, so every capture is the no-transcoder half of the design: the library says so, and the video that was published is poster_only.",
 "_poster": "The poster comes out of the Media Library and has no file input of its own. poster-picker-* is the popup, poster-picked-* is the chosen image. Its thumbnail does not load in these captures: Media::urlFor() builds from site_url (APP_URL), and this preview is served from 127.0.0.1:8471 -- a preview artefact, not a defect, and the adoption itself succeeded (the published row reads poster_only).",
